---
// Real wg-quick config — every value here is what the actual controller
// emits in handlers/devices.go via wireguard.GenerateDeviceConfig:
//   * 10.100.0.X/16 overlay
//   * MTU 1420 (set in addPeerCommon)
//   * Endpoint = config.DOMAIN (operator-provided)
//   * PersistentKeepalive = 25 (default in addPeerCommon)
// The private-key + public-key strings are clearly marked as placeholders.
---

<section style="background: var(--bg-2);">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-eyebrow">Honest engineering</div>
    <h2 class="sec-h">It's a wg-quick config. No agent. No daemon.</h2>
    <p class="sec-lede">
      The controller generates standard WireGuard configuration. You paste
      it into your router's existing WireGuard interface — the same one
      TP-Link, MikroTik, OpenWrt and Ubiquiti already ship. The router
      keeps doing what it does. MeshWG just brokers the tunnel.
    </p>

    <div class="config-shell">
      <div class="config-side">
        <h3>What it doesn't do</h3>
        <p>
          MeshWG is not a Cisco competitor. It doesn't replace firmware,
          run an agent on your AP, or invent a new tunnel protocol.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><svg class="i" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>Standard WireGuard — works on any router that supports it.</li>
          <li><svg class="i" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>You own the config. Export it. Audit it. Run it without MeshWG.</li>
          <li><svg class="i" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>Private keys are generated at peer creation and never leave the controller's encrypted store.</li>
          <li><svg class="i" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 13l4 4L19 7"/></svg>If the controller is down, existing tunnels keep running — kernel WireGuard doesn't depend on it.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <pre class="config-pre"><span class="c"># wg0.conf — generated by the controller for site "branch-mumbai"</span>
<span class="h">[Interface]</span>
PrivateKey = <span class="v">(generated by controller, returned once)</span>
Address    = <span class="v">10.100.0.2/16</span>
MTU        = <span class="v">1420</span>

<span class="h">[Peer]</span>
<span class="c"># controller's hub for tenant "acme-networks"</span>
PublicKey           = <span class="v">&lt;tenant hub public key&gt;</span>
Endpoint            = <span class="v">vpn.your-domain.com:51820</span>
AllowedIPs          = <span class="v">10.100.0.0/16</span>
PersistentKeepalive = <span class="v">25</span></pre>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .config-shell {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 28px;
    margin-top: 48px; align-items: start;
  }
  .config-side h3 { font-size: 22px; letter-spacing: -.01em; margin: 0 0 12px; }
  .config-side p  { color: var(--text-2); font-size: 15px; margin: 0 0 18px; }
  .config-side ul { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; }
  .config-side li { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; color: var(--text-2); font-size: 14px; }
  .config-side li .i {
    flex: 0 0 18px; margin-top: 2px;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .config-pre {
    background: #0a0a0a;
    color: #ededed;
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    padding: 20px 22px;
    font: 12.5px/1.7 var(--font-mono);
    overflow: auto;
    border: 1px solid #1f1f1f;
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-code);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .config-pre .h { color: #a5b4fc; }
  .config-pre .c { color: #6b7280; }
  .config-pre .v { color: #fcd34d; }

  @media (max-width: 980px) {
    .config-shell { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
